  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bolivia Libre de Malaria Para Vivir Bien - Bolivia (Plurinational State) (01-Mar-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bolivia (Plurinational State), Malaria, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Bolivia)This program has the following goals: Eliminate indigenous transmission of P. falciparum by 2019.  Interrupt indigenous transmission of P vivax in the 15 priority low-endemicity municipalities and prevent the reintroduction of malaria into transmission-free municipalities in the five municipalities in the departments of Chuquisaca, Santa Cruz, Tarija.  Reduce the number of P. vivax cases by 50&#xa0;percent in the 21 endemic municipalities in the departments of Pando, Beni and La Paz.. The objectives of this program are: Guarantee immediate universal access to high-quality diagnosis, treatment and monitoring of malaria..  Monitoring and evaluation of activities established in the NSP for malaria..  Promote, strengthen and optimize the mechanisms and tools for vector control.</narrative>
  </description>
